      {
        "id": 20510,
        "name": "scruffyrogue",
        "username": "scruffyrogue",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-01-16T03:25:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've been binging the youtube videos of gameplay since I got my copy of the game and I have a question about how the Minion Maker's Upgrade Minion ability is supposed to work. The pertinent bit is that you can upgrade a minion to your Max die size, replacing its minion form.</p>\n<p>I had assumed this meant take your Max and look on the chart on pg 87 (rolled an 8 on your max, get a d10!). But in the video from last year it seemed like the Floral Fantom just took the die size of whatever rolled the highest value and turned her minion into that (a d12 in this case). Though of course it's possible I misunderstood the exact dice mechanics they were using. And it's also possible the rules have changed since that was filmed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Can someone clarify how this is supposed to work?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Thanks....</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:38.166Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 113,
        "reads": 10,
        "readers_count": 9,
        "score": 567.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 20508,
        "topic_slug": "minion-maker-upgrade-minion",
        "display_username": "scruffyrogue",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I've been binging the youtube videos of gameplay since I got my copy of the game and I have a question about how the Minion Maker's Upgrade Minion ability is supposed to work. The pertinent bit is that you can upgrade a minion to your Max die size, replacing its minion form.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I had assumed this meant take your Max and look on the chart on pg 87 (rolled an 8 on your max, get a d10!). But in the video from last year it seemed like the Floral Fantom just took the die size of whatever rolled the highest value and turned her minion into that (a d12 in this case). Though of course it's possible I misunderstood the exact dice mechanics they were using. And it's also possible the rules have changed since that was filmed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Can someone clarify how this is supposed to work?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thanks....</p>",
